---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About — Harsh"
  description="About Harsh and his systems programming journey."
>
  <main class="article">

    <div class="eyebrow">about</div>

    <h1>Hi, I'm Harsh.</h1>

    <div class="article-content">

      <p>
        I'm learning how things work below the abstractions.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most of my time goes into Rust, systems programming,
        concurrency, memory, operating systems and performance.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm particularly interested in the places where software
        meets hardware — where a seemingly simple line of code
        turns into memory ordering, cache behaviour, syscalls,
        page tables or a surprisingly complicated bug.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm also building things while I learn.
      </p>

      <p>
        One of them is
        <a href="https://github.com/harshsys0x/haphazard">
          haphazard
        </a>,
        a lightweight hazard-pointer library for Rust.
      </p>

      <p>
        This site is where I write down what I learn along the way.
      </p>

    </div>

  </main>
</Layout>